{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1149830-homebrew-legacies-2e","id":1149830,"title":"Homebrew Legacies (2E)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-14T19:58:10-07:00","id":1149830,"title":"Homebrew Legacies (2E)","content":"So, here are some Legacies I homebrewed for 2E. Most of them are not totally done, but I hope to be able to wrap them all pretty soon.<br /> <br /> Some of the Attainments are based on homebrewed spells from the thread &quot;Creative Thaumaturgy: Fallen World Edition&quot;. You'll find those spells and the mention of their authors here: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1H0BBs20Ta9RKnWirld02c8GiWoRGU5gTb9QvljIOCw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> Let me know what you think !<br /> <br /> ------------<br /> <br /> <b>The Untouchables: Acanthus (Matter/Fate), Free Council/Seers of the Throne.</b><br /> A single Legacy split in two by the Great Refusal, it is composed of mages who dissimulate behind a guise of poverty or inferiority to test the goodness of those around them: those siding with the Free Council truly believe in the power of selflessness, while those serving the Throne only feign to uphold those tenets to keep the masses in their blissful mediocrity.<br /> <br /> Link: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sRnB5fFE1TeUmjipvURKGFrvHhbRaBjieQE_Wzscmf4/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Wei Jie : Acanthus (Prime/Fate), Seers of the Throne. </b><br /> The perfect bait for Mysteries-hungry Diamond Mages, the Wei Jie infiltrate the Orders by playing the part of the mysterious, charged. Their Nimbus flare far brighter than their real Gnosis should allow, their Pattern is full of intricate dead-ends, prophecies and visions seem to all revolve around them\u2026 but this is nothing more than smoke and mirrors, carefully crafted by those occult honeypots.<br /> <br /> <b>The Engravers of Convolution: Acanthus (Space/Fate), Seers of the Throne.</b><br /> According to the beliefs of this Legacy, the Watchtowers weren\u2019t created by the Oracles as beacons, but as mausoleums, where they entombed magic so that a cataclysm such as the Fall would never happen again. Each Awakened Soul has violated the peace of these tombs, and is thus stricken by a personal Malediction. The Engravers learn how to decipher that individual Curse, and how to use it to enact a fitting punishment to the unworthy.<br /> .<br /> <b>The Outpacers: Mastigos (Time/Mind), Adamantine Arrow.</b><br /> Out of their belief that every mundane distraction is an attempt from the Exarchs to thwart the mages of the Diamond, they serve their fellow mage by handling mundane business for them, using their Attainments to do so at a preternatural speed.<br /> <br /> Link: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/19ImYI-EonC9Fo64U2kkQxZXiedtqEKSeZnZsRS-pVgY/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> <b>Der Kreis Der Jungfrau: Moros (Life/Matter), Guardians of the Veil.</b><br /> Centered around the Jungfrau, a ghostly female apparition from the Germanic medieval folklore who embodies the Dark Plague, this Legacy learn its members resistance and dominance over all things poisonous, either biological or chemical.<br /> <br /> <b>The Syringe: Moros (Mind/Death), Mysterium/Seers of the Throne.</b><br /> Created following the numerous clashes between Kindred and Seers, those mages act as enforcers of the Exarchs\u2019 Law on vampiric Domains: they extract and inject what they want from the Cacophony, just like their namesake extract or inject components from a subject\u2019s blood.<br /> <br /> <b>The Arrangers of the Scorching Fire: Obrimos (Spirits/Prime), Silver Ladder.</b><br /> This Middle-Eastern Legacy is notorious for its mediatory role between the theist vision of most Obrimos and the animist paradigm of most Thyrsus. Their Attainments revolve particularly around the phenomenon of Resonance, common to both Mana and Essence.<br /> <br /> <b>The Red Clergy of Rhllor: Obrimos (Death/Forces), Seers of the Throne.</b><br /> Bantis z\u014dbrie issa se oss\u0233ngnoti l\u0113dys. (Because Night is dark and full of terrors).<br /> <br /> Link: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1XfgTUJ_b3_Ddd6A4VGZiwDzjx2Z1297k-1ccDF1Y9mk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> <b>The Karawoorii, equally known as the Parters of the Halves: Thyrsus (Spirits/Life), Mysterium or Guardians of the Veil.</b><br /> After being force to sacrifice their inner closeness to the Shadow due to a scheme of the Seers of the Throne, those Shamans bargained with Hosts Spirits and gained power over the Nether Realm, a place that doesn\u2019t lie on either side of the Gauntlet, but inside of it.<br /> <br /> Link:<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ZpjT0YxNQYIF5GSZW3vM8swUfcYXGjBrULYIDrKrH0k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","user":"Adrasalieth","date":". 10-15-2017, 06:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","name":"Adrasalieth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}